    "notes": {
      "en|situation.sumter_evacuated.text|terms": "The record's terms, quoted and attributed to Beauregard's offer of 11 April (OR I-1 p. 13), which Anderson's telegram of 18 April (p. 12) names as the terms he accepted; a surrender on terms, as 0074 allows a capture notice to state it. The garrison left under terms and was never captured, and Anderson keeps serving. Text only, no effects; it fires only on the evacuated_under_terms token at fort_sumter."
    }
  },
